  "diagnosis": {
    "summary": "Both failed checks equate the application-level sys.executable file hash with the OS process image hash. In these two Windows venv-launched workers the saved sys.executable-derived digest equals the frozen venv launcher, while every retained-handle OS image/path digest for the authenticated actual worker equals the distinct frozen base interpreter.",
    "evidence_status": "Explained by immutable saved receipts and the frozen publish_identity/auditor sources. The literal full sys.executable string was intentionally not logged; its source-derived digest and basename are recorded. No fresh interpreter/OS probe was performed.",
    "root_cause": "The frozen auditor assumes a worker self-reported executable hash must be the OS base image hash. That assumption is invalid for this observed launcher/base split. Its synthetic fixture always sets worker/helper self hash to base_python and therefore does not exercise this Windows venv behavior. Producer admission independently validates the retained OS image/path/hash, so producer.passed and frozen audit.passed answer different checks.",
    "source_references": [
      {
        "path": "experiments/process_observer_probe.py",
        "line": 84,
        "fact": "publish_identity hashes sys.executable at lines86–87; it does not derive an OS image hash."
      },
      {
        "path": "scripts/audit_child_image_census.py",
        "line": 75,
        "fact": "base_worker_self_hash requires ready runtime_executable_sha256 == frozen base_python."
      },
      {
        "path": "experiments/child_image_census.py",
        "line": 69,
        "fact": "image_identity queries QueryFullProcessImageNameW from the retained handle, hashes that path and rechecks PID/creation."
      },
      {
        "path": "tests/test_child_image_census_auditor.py",
        "line": 21,
        "fact": "Synthetic ready() assigns base_python hash to every worker/helper self receipt."
      }
    ],
